3. Analyze the Throughput Graph (3–4 lines)
Use this example as your assignment explanation, adjusting it to match your actual graph.
The throughput graph shows how many requests the server processes over time.
A steady increase indicates that the server is handling more requests as the load grows. 
A plateau may indicate that the server has reached its processing capacity, while sudden drops may indicate delays, errors, or resource bottlenecks.
The graph should be compared with response times and error rates before concluding that the server is overloaded.
